</div></div></div>

<div class="topic" data-i="4"><button class="th" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span class="ic"><svg><use href="#i14"/></svg></span><span><b>The Fellowship examination</b><small>Three kinds of station over 2 days</small></span><span class="ch"></span></button><div class="pn"><p>Held over 2 days, from the end of November to early December. It has three kinds of station.</p>
<div class="grid2"><div class="cs-card"><h3>Patient-based OSCE</h3><p>A real or standardised patient is present.</p></div><div class="cs-card"><h3>Patientless OSCE</h3><p>Photographs, imaging, investigations or other materials. Introduced because the number of candidates increased.</p></div><div class="cs-card"><h3>Viva voce</h3><p>An oral examination of depth and breadth of specialty knowledge.</p></div></div>
<p>Details are in Module 6.</p></div></div>

<div class="topic" data-i="5"><button class="th" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span class="ic"><svg><use href="#i5"/></svg></span><span><b>Comparing the formats</b><small>Online, patient-based, patientless, viva</small></span><span class="ch"></span></button><div class="pn"><div class="scroll cs-card"><table>
<tr><th>Feature</th><th>Online OSCE</th><th>Patient-based OSCE</th><th>Patientless OSCE</th><th>Viva voce</th></tr>
<tr><td>Setting</td><td>Secure online platform</td><td>Examination room</td><td>Skills lab</td><td>Quiet room</td></tr>
<tr><td>Patient</td><td>None</td><td>Real or simulated</td><td>None; models and equipment</td><td>None</td></tr>
<tr><td>Interaction</td><td>Via computer screen</td><td>Face to face</td><td>Hands-on</td><td>Verbal discussion</td></tr>
<tr><td>Assessment focus</td><td>Reasoning, knowledge, interpretation</td><td>Communication, examination, management</td><td>Technical skills, procedures</td><td>Knowledge, reasoning, judgement</td></tr>
<tr><td>Limit</td><td>Limited physical examination</td><td>Needs trained patients and logistics</td><td>Less realistic</td><td>No practical skills</td></tr></table></div></div></div>

<div class="topic" data-i="6"><button class="th" type="button" aria-expanded="false"><span class="ic"><svg><use href="#i4"/></svg></span><span><b>Why the formats changed</b><small>Candidate growth 2015 to 2025</small></span><span class="ch"></span></button><div class="pn"><p>Between 2015 and 2025 the number of Part II candidates grew about 249%, from 91 to 318, an average of about 13.3% a year.</p>
